## Summary

Implements #2804 - Refactored `SocketHTTP_URI_decode` to reduce deeply nested conditionals from 5 levels down to 2 levels.

## Changes

- **Extracted helper function**: `decode_percent_char()` handles RFC 3986 §2.1 percent-encoded character decoding with guard clauses
- **Consolidated bounds checks**: Moved output buffer overflow check outside if/else chain (DRY principle)
- **Improved readability**: Clear separation between validation logic and character decoding
- **Added documentation**: Doxygen comments explain the helper function's purpose and contract

## Before (5 levels of nesting)

```c
for (size_t i = 0; i < len; i++)           /* Level 1: Loop */
  {
    if (input[i] == '%')                   /* Level 2: Percent encoding */
      {
        if (i + 2 >= len)                  /* Level 3: Bounds check */
          return -1;

        if (hi == HEX_INVALID || lo == HEX_INVALID)  /* Level 4: Hex validation */
          return -1;

        if (out_len + 1 > output_size)     /* Level 5: Output bounds */
          return -1;
        // ... decode logic
      }
    else if (input[i] == '+')
      {
        if (out_len + 1 > output_size)
          return -1;
        // ... plus handling
      }
    // ... etc
  }
```

## After (2 levels of nesting)

```c
for (size_t i = 0; i < len; i++)
  {
    /* Guard: Check output buffer space before writing */
    if (out_len + 1 > output_size)
      return -1;

    if (input[i] == '%')
      {
        unsigned char decoded;
        if (decode_percent_char (input, len, i, &decoded) != 0)
          return -1;

        output[out_len++] = (char)decoded;
        i += 2; /* Skip the two hex digits */
      }
    else if (input[i] == '+')
      {
        output[out_len++] = ' ';
      }
    else
      {
        output[out_len++] = input[i];
      }
  }
```

