## Summary

Implements #2833

Reduces nesting from 5 levels to 3 levels in `http2_recombine_cookie_headers` function.

## Changes

- **Extracted helper function**: `is_cookie_header()` encapsulates the cookie header check
- **Early continue pattern**: Non-cookie headers are skipped immediately with `continue`
- **Improved readability**: Main logic is now at normal indentation (level 3) instead of buried deep (level 5)
- **Clear comments**: Each section is clearly labeled for maintainability

## Before (5 levels)

```c
for (size_t i = 0; i < *count; i++)                                    /* Level 2 */
  {
    const SocketHPACK_Header *h = &headers[i];
    if (h->name_len == STRLEN_LIT ("cookie")                           /* Level 3 */
        && memcmp (h->name, "cookie", STRLEN_LIT ("cookie")) == 0)
      {
        cookie_indices[num_cookies] = i;                               /* Level 4 */
        if (first_cookie_idx == (size_t)-1)                            /* Level 5 */
          first_cookie_idx = i;
        total_value_len += h->value_len;
        num_cookies++;
      }
  }
```

## After (3 levels)

```c
for (size_t i = 0; i < *count; i++)
  {
    const SocketHPACK_Header *h = &headers[i];

    /* Skip non-cookie headers early */
    if (!is_cookie_header (h))
      continue;

    /* Record first cookie index on first encounter */
    if (first_cookie_idx == (size_t)-1)                               /* Level 3 */
      first_cookie_idx = i;

    /* Accumulate cookie data */
    cookie_indices[num_cookies] = i;
    total_value_len += h->value_len;
    num_cookies++;
  }
```

## Test Plan

- [x] All 128 tests pass with sanitizers (ASan + UBSan)
- [x] HTTP/2 integration tests pass
- [x] No functional changes, purely structural refactoring

